Z||000010||btoth||12-19-2001||12:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>ejayerik has aome interesting points. <P>I wish it was like in the "old days", when there weren't chemicals and crap on everything. I wish we could eat stuff as God intended; fresh and free of "extra" stuff, chemicals and such. <P>I also eat regular store-bought food, but it does bug me. <P>It'd be nice not to have to eat some chemical company's homework for dinner. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Definatly!  I agree.  It's even more pathetic that they add a million vitamins and nutrients to things that normally would have none.  And tell me why a serving of sugar-covered cereal needs to have 100% of every vitamin and mineral artificially added to it to make it "good for you".  Maybe if they tried removing all the sugar and fake colors and flavors people would just eat the things that really had nutritional values in the first place.<P>And who wants to eat all the pesticides and things sprayed on fuits and vegitables?  And who wants to eat meat that's been injected with drugs to make the meet tender and moist???  That's just sick.  (Like turkey injected with tenderizers and salts.)||||reg||1
