Z||000012||frontal lobe||12-19-2001||02:34 PM||||The people that want to eat all the food with pesticides on it, and eat the animal products with hormones, are the ones that want inexpensive food.<P>People SAY they wish the food was "natural" and organic, but they also want it to cost the same.  Well, that doesn't happen.  The yield isn't as great.  The labor costs are higher.  So which do you want?<P>BTW, I am quite certain people in Afghanistan, Somalia, Ethiopia, and hundreds of other places in the world would be more than happy to eat our "pesticide and hormone laden" food, and not have all this angst and hand-wringing that we have.  I suspect they would find this whole topic quite amusing and ludicrous.<P>Also, make no mistake about PETA people.  They are only involving human health issues into the topic as an end to a means.  They don't care one bit about the human, they care about the ANIMAL.  They just try to use the proposed human health benefit as a motivation for people to leave their beloved animals alone.<P>Disclaimer:  I AM NOT for the intentional abuse of animals.||||reg||1
Z||000013||DaRkLoRD||12-19-2001||03:11 PM||||there is absolutely no reason we have to be eating food covered in pesticides, pumped full of artificial hormones, extra vitamins, etc..<P>We studied this in my biotech class last semester, and when I started that class, I had very little idea about how much garbage we're eating.. after the semester was done however, I realized we're making ourselves sick. So many of our health problems are aggravated (if not caused outright) by the unhealthy foods we eat.. I became interested in hydroponics after studying this, and learning what kinds of yields a properly maintained hydroponic garden can produce.. so, as a project, I built one.. it's in my basement right now, with about 8 tomato plants growing very nicely.. each plant is expected to yield about 10-20lbs of tomatos over the growing season. I used organic seeds, pure water, and hydroponic vegetable nutrients from a plant store. When you factor in how much this has cost me, for this growing season, it would have been far cheaper to buy tomatos.. but now that I have this setup, for future crops I just need to buy seeds and nutrient solution.. and at $20 for 2 huge bottles.. that's dirt cheap.<BR>commercial hydroponic farms are becoming more common, but still not very widespread when compared to traditional farms with their tractors and liquid manure spreaders and pesticides.....<P>as for meat.. biotech researchers have already cloned certain types of cells.. bone marrow, skin, etc.. so why not beef and chicken muscle tissue? meat cubes! same taste, optimum conditions.. and nothing had to die to put it on your plate.. everyone should be happy.. except those who think cloning is evil... (it has the potential for very nasty stuff, but I don't think meat cubes would be too likely to take over the world....)<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000014||frontal lobe||12-19-2001||03:32 PM||||DaRkLoRD, I applaud you.  Seriously.  So the following comments are not a slam, or really even a "rebuttal".  However, take your plants outdoors where the insects are and factor that into the yield.  Because that is where the amount of food to feed the population would be.<P>I read the "Little House on the Prairie" books to my 6 y.o. daughter every night before bed.  We currently are in "On the Banks of Plum Creek", when they moved to Minnesota and Pa planted a big wheat field and was planning on all the things he could buy with the profit.  Last night's chapter, however, was the odd cloud that was coming toward them.  It was a MASSIVE cloud of grasshoppers that landed, stayed for about 3-4 days, and ate EVERY SINGLE GREEN THING.  EVERYTHING.<P>Hmmm.  I wonder why that doesn't happen anymore.<P>Disclaimer number 2:  I am not pro-chemicals.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Earl||12-19-2001||05:05 PM||||  I don't belive for one minute that Peta cares about the welfare of animals .As far as I can tell all they care about is POWER. The power to force their utopian Ideas onto everyone .They feel that they are the only ones moral enough to decide what we do and how we act.Just like the seara club and all other "environmental wackoes" If we are to belive what they say. We shouldn't have cured half of the illnesses we have and we shouldn't live near wild areas, how ever this whole planet was once wilderness .<BR>  So what are we supposed to do Quit eating animals, drinking milk, driving cars,  burning fossil fuels, building and operating nuclear power plants, building homes, farming, and mining, basically everything we do "hurts the ecosystem" and animals.<BR>  I quit drinking milk as soon as I could tell my mother "I DON'T LIKE MILK!" that is my choice so I guess I should be weak well I am not. I have been a welder for 15 years I work hard and have never broken a bone .<BR>  I don't care if you drink milk or eat meat and you shouldn't care, that is your choice and that is what really ticks them off ,they can't control you . <BR>  I have seen the incredibly stupid things people do, in the name of protecting the animals. They act like SPOILED CRYBABY CHILDREN!<BR>  I just wish they would realize humans are a part of nature .<BR>  ONLY THE STRONG SURVIVE.||||reg||1
Z||000016||DaRkLoRD||12-19-2001||06:45 PM||||humans are a part of nature. however most of our technology is not.<P>we *are* slowly destroying ourselves.. I'm not a member of any organization like this, and I think many of them are excessively radical.. but I do understand <B>part</B> of where they're coming from..<P>people aren't going to give up their cars easily.. I know I wouldn't.. but we could switch to alcohol fuels... it can be made incredibly cheap, as alcohol can be made from anything that will ferment.. rotton fruit anyone??? if there was a large scale move to the use of alcohol in our cars resulting in lower costs and increased availablity, the average levels of pollution would drop drastically.. and our cars would make more power to boot. the only extra initial cost to us is changing the engine seals and hoses to silicone.<P>there are alternatives that aren't that radical.. but would still make a world of difference.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
