Z||000029||Mach10||12-20-2001||07:27 PM||||Yes... Colostrum is a GOOD thing...<P>I don't advocate CRUELTY to animals. But farming is not cruel. What do you want to DO with the cattle? The last "wild" cattle died out thousands of years ago... You can't set them free... <P>I have no problems eating meat. You made me slaughter my own animals? I'd STILL have no problem. It's reasonably humane, in most plants. The jackhammer to the head usually does it the first time... After that, it's bled out. The violent twitching and thrashing is a nervous response to the brain losing blood. Same with throat-slitting. relatively painless, and VERY quick. <P>PETA is a group composed of "feel-good" hippies. Unwilling to take any responsibility for what's wrong with the world today, they run around on pointless crusades, blissfully unaware that they are the root cause of all the harm, and that by not eating meat does not absolve oneself from responsibility. <P>Eating meat is NOT wrong. If you don't like it, don't eat it. But don't you DARE push that on me... I'm hungry, and they are better off dead anyway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>||||reg||12
